# demo-workflow – project context

Single GitHub Actions workflow: `.github/workflows/desco_balance_notifier.yml`
(daily 00:00 UTC = 6 AM BDT, plus manual `workflow_dispatch`). It fetches the DESCO prepaid
meter balance and notifies via Gmail (SMTP) and Discord webhook. The SMS step is commented out
on purpose; do not re-enable unless asked.

## Auth + balance (working since 2026-11-09)
DESCO replaced the public balance endpoint (`/api/tkdes/customer/getBalance` → 401
`AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED`). The workflow now logs in and reads the daily snapshot:

1. `GET /api/auth/csrf` → `XSRF-TOKEN` cookie (URL-decode; send as `X-XSRF-TOKEN` on POSTs)
2. `POST /api/auth/login` body `{"username","password"}` (phone number works as username)
3. `GET /api/accounts` → pick linked account (`DESCO_METER_NO` / `DESCO_ACCOUNT_NO` filters;
   meter `661120233559` / accountNo `17002101` is the linked one)
4. `GET /api/accounts/<accountId>/balance` → `.balance` (daily snapshot, not live)

Prefer the daily snapshot over `POST .../realtime-balance` (rate-limited). Fail loudly if
balance is not numeric. Never commit or paste session cookies/passwords.

Notifications use a compact JSON summary (accountNo, meterNo, balance, currency,
balanceSnapshotAt, stale, etc.). Do not dump full API `consumerMessages` into shell steps —
multiline Bangla text breaks `${{ env.* }}` interpolation (Discord failed that way once).

## Secrets used
DESCO_USER, DESCO_PASS, EMAIL_USER, EMAIL_PASS, DISCORD_WEBHOOK
(SMS_API_KEY only if SMS is re-enabled).

